Curr Biol</source><year>2003</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>219</fpage><lpage>223</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12573217</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00012-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cremer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sledge</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Heinze</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Male ants disguised by the queen's bouquet</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2002</year><volume>419</volume><fpage>897</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12410300</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/419897a</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Garant</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Dodson</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernatchez</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Differential reproductive success and heritability of alternative reproductive tactics in wild Atlantic salmon (<italic>Salmo salar </italic>L.)</article-title><source>Evolution</source><year>2003</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>1133</fpage><lpage>1141</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12836829</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greeff</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferguson</surname><given-names>JWH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mating ecology of the nonpollinating fig wasps of <italic>Ficus ingens</italic></article-title><source>Anim Behav</source><year>1999</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>215</fpage><lpage>222</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10053089</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/anbe.1998.0954</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hunt</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Simmons</surname><given-names>LW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Status-dependent selection in the dimorphic beetle <italic>Onthophagus taurus</italic></article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B</source><year>2001</year><volume>268</volume><fpage>2409</fpage><lpage>2414</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1098/rspb.2001.1758</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dominey</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Alternative mating tactics and evolutionarily stable strategies</article-title><source>Amer Zool</source><year>1984</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>385</fpage><lpage>396</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Cremer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Heinze</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Live and let die: why fighter males of the ant <italic>Cardiocondyla</italic> kill each other but tolerate their winged rivals</article-title><source>Behav Ecol</source><year>2002</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>54</fpage><lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/beheco/14.1.54</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tsuji</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamauchi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamamura</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A mathematical model for wing dimorphism in male <italic>Cardiocondyla</italic> ants</article-title><source>J Ethol</source><year>1994</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF02350076</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bourke</surname><given-names>AFG</given-names></name><name><surname>Franks</surname><given-names>NR</given-names></name></person-group><source>Social evolution in ants</source><year>1995</year><publisher-name>Princeton, Princeton University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wheeler</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Developmental and physiological determinants of caste in social Hymenoptera: evolutionary implications</article-title><source>Am Nat</source><year>1986</year><volume>128</volume><fpage>13</fpage><lpage>34</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/284536</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>EO</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Insect Societies</source><year>1971</year><publisher-name>Cambridge, Mass., Harvard University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schrempf</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Heinze</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Cremer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sexual cooperation: mating increases longevity in ant queens</article-title><source>Curr Biol</source><year>2005</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>267</fpage><lpage>270</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15694312</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heinze</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><